. /********************************************************************
> Three-way test using HOUSEHOLD-LEVEL PSU social composition
> CORRECTED FOR NFHS-4 vs NFHS-5 HOUSEHOLD VARIABLE NAMES
> 
> IMPORTANT CODING DIFFERENCE
> ---------------------------
> NFHS-4 household recode:
>     religion of household head      = sh34
>     caste/tribe type of HH head     = sh36
> 
>     sh34:
>         1 Hindu
>         2 Muslim
>         3 Christian
>         4 Sikh
>         5 Buddhist/Neo-Buddhist
>         6 Jain
>         ...
> 
>     sh36:
>         1 Scheduled caste
>         2 Scheduled tribe
>         3 Other Backward Class
>         4 None of above
>         8 Don't know
> 
> NFHS-5 household recode:
>     religion of household head      = sh47
>     caste/tribe type of HH head     = sh49
> 
> The NFHS-5 coding below follows your existing project code.
> 
> Question:
> Does the comparison-group vs Forward Hindu difference in the
> private-public neonatal mortality gap vary with household-based
> PSU social composition?
> 
> Preferred composition measure:
>     leave-one-HOUSEHOLD-out weighted PSU share
> 
> Console output only.
> ********************************************************************/
. 
. clear all
{res}{txt}
{com}. set more off
{txt}
{com}. set maxvar 7000

{txt}
{com}. 
. 
